<title>USA: MBIA qualifies six issues for bond insurance.</title>
<headline>MBIA qualifies six issues for bond insurance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>MBIA Insurance Corp said on Wednesday that it qualified the following six municipal bond issues, which will be sold competitively, for insurance.</p>
<p>--Oakland, Calif., $45.42 million General Obligation (GO) bonds.</p>
<p>--Westfield, Ind., $8 million sewer works revenue bonds.</p>
<p>--St.Paul, Minn., $17.5 million GOs capital improvement bonds and $2.45 million GOs street bonds.</p>
<p>--Willmar ISD #347, Minn., $20.66 million GOs refunding bonds</p>
<p>--Spartanburg County, S.C., School District, $11.6 million GOs.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
